      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.27,
      "end_seconds": 23.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.09,
      "end_seconds": 31.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "yeah, it's cramping in my calves when I walk. I don't know what's causing it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.32,
      "end_seconds": 35.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.67,
      "end_seconds": 40.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "it's been like this since this morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.08,
      "end_seconds": 45.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.33,
      "end_seconds": 55.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.56,
      "text": "It's worse with walking. I'd call it mild. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.85,
      "end_seconds": 62.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Has there been hair loss on your shins too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.21,
      "end_seconds": 65.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "ah, yes, for six months"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.0,
      "end_seconds": 78.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.8,
      "end_seconds": 86.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Actually, no, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.7,
      "end_seconds": 100.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Okay, what's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.09,
      "end_seconds": 110.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.4,
      "end_seconds": 114.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.56,
      "end_seconds": 125.71,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "I swim twice a week. My partner and our baby. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.47,
      "end_seconds": 130.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.48,
      "end_seconds": 133.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "yes, diabetes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.05,
      "end_seconds": 144.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Yes, diabetes is known to us, good to have that clear. Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.25,
      "end_seconds": 149.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "I mean, my uncle has high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.95,
      "end_seconds": 162.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "have you noticed chest pain, fever or back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.12,
      "end_seconds": 169.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "no chest pain, fever or back pain, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.51,
      "end_seconds": 174.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.18,
      "end_seconds": 180.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.1,
      "end_seconds": 183.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.62,
      "end_seconds": 197.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.24,
      "end_seconds": 225.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 97 percent, temp 36.9 degrees, pressure 113 over 74, pulse 85."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.49,
      "end_seconds": 249.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.27,
      "text": "so, based on your history, I'd lean towards peripheral arterial disease. I think a cholesterol test makes sense here, for arterial disease"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.33,
      "end_seconds": 253.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "right, uh, understood"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.48,
      "end_seconds": 276.56,
      "duration_seconds": 22.08,
      "text": "I want an ankle-brachial index done, that's for claudication. What I'm giving you is clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day, long term. That should help with arterial disease. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. We'll refer you to the vascular clinic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.04,
      "end_seconds": 278.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.06,
      "end_seconds": 306.06,
      "duration_seconds": 26.0,
      "text": "Let's hold off on an ultrasound of the leg arteries for now, and if there's no change in two weeks we can revisit it. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. I'd like you back in four weeks. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.66,
      "end_seconds": 309.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.55,
      "end_seconds": 311.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
